# Projects

Work in this repo happens in a **project**. There are two: **Thalos** (default)
and **Earth**. The generator itself is shared; a project is the named world
you are working on — its pins, seed, and fixture.

- Thalos is the world being discovered. Development, `bun run preview`,
  `bun run sheet`, and `bun run export:td` run against it unless Earth is
  asked for.
- Earth is the present-day reference fixture. Use `--earth` or
  `--project=earth`, or `bun run check:earth`.
- Pins live in `src/projects/`. Loading a project assigns the whole set; it
  does not merge with the last one. Thalos gains a pin when something is
  decided.
- A project also owns its artifacts: `preview/<name>/`. Captures, crops
  and 90 m preview bakes belong to that project and seed. Loading another
  project must not show the last one's tiles. The preview folder holds
  only project directories.
- Do not treat the generator's Earth-calibrated DEFAULTS as a third project.
  Those are the unmarked baseline the pins sit on.
